{"title": "Sectional Mock #25 (Mixed)", "duration_min": 30.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p> Three friends A, B and C started the business investing in the ratio 2 : 4 : 7. If after every 3 month A doubled his capital and B halved his capital. If the capital of C remained same and the profit earned by C after 1 years is Rs. 4200, then by what percentage profit shared by B is less than the profit shared by A? </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2350;&#2367;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; A, B &#2324;&#2352; C &#2344;&#2375; 2:4:7 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2352;&#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2357;&#2360;&#2366;&#2351; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; 3 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; A&#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2346;&#2370;&#2306;&#2332;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2379;&#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; B &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2346;&#2370;&#2306;&#2332;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; C &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2370;&#2306;&#2332;&#2368; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2352;&#2361;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; 1 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; C &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; 4200 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379;, B &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2360;&#2366;&#2333;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349;, A &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2360;&#2366;&#2333;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2325;&#2350; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["64%", "62.5%", "78.25%", "75%"], "options_hi": ["64%", "62.5%", "78.25%", "75%"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "\"<p>According to the question</p><p>Ratio of investment of A, B and C = 2 : 4 : 7</p><p>Let the investment of A, B and C be 200 units, 400 units and 700 units respectively</p><p>Effective investment of A = 200 &#215; 3 + 400 &#215; 3 + 800 &#215; 3 +1600 &#215; 3 = 9000</p><p>Effective investment of B = 400 &#215; 3 + 200 &#215; 3 + 100 &#215; 3 + 50 &#215; 3 = 2250</p><p>Effective investment of C = 700 &#215; 12 = 8400</p><p>We know that ratio of profit is equal to the ratio of product of capital and time</p><p>A : B : C = 9000 : 2250 : 8400 = 180 : 45 : 168</p><p>168 units = Rs. 4200</p><p>1 units = 25</p><p>Profit of A = Rs. 4500</p><p>Profit of B = Rs. 1125</p><p>Required percentage = ((Profit of A) &#8211; (profit of B)/(profit of A)) &#215; 100</p><p> Required percentage = \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-000303.png\"/>\r </p>\"", "solution_hi": "\"<p>According to the question</p><p>Ratio of investment of A, B and C = 2 : 4 : 7</p><p>Let the investment of A, B and C be 200 units, 400 units and 700 units respectively</p><p>Effective investment of A = 200 &#215; 3 + 400 &#215; 3 + 800 &#215; 3 +1600 &#215; 3 = 9000</p><p>Effective investment of B = 400 &#215; 3 + 200 &#215; 3 + 100 &#215; 3 + 50 &#215; 3 = 2250</p><p>Effective investment of C = 700 &#215; 12 = 8400</p><p>We know that ratio of profit is equal to the ratio of product of capital and time</p><p>A : B : C = 9000 : 2250 : 8400 = 180 : 45 : 168</p><p>168 units = Rs. 4200</p><p>1 units = 25</p><p>Profit of A = Rs. 4500</p><p>Profit of B = Rs. 1125</p><p>Required percentage = ((Profit of A) &#8211; (profit of B)/(profit of A)) &#215; 100</p><p> Required percentage = \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-000303.png\"/>\r </p>\"", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>If (X + 2) and (X  -  1) is the factor of (2X<sup>3</sup> + 12X<sup>2</sup> + mX + n), the value of m and n are:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; (X + 2) &#2324;&#2352; (X - 1) (2X<sup>3</sup> + 12X<sup>2</sup> + mX + n) &#2325;&#2366; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2344;&#2326;&#2306;&#2337; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; m &#2324;&#2352; n &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;:</p>", "options_en": ["m = 6, n = -20", "m = -6, n = 20", "m = -6, n = 44", "m = 6, n = -44"], "options_hi": ["m = 6, n = -20", "m = -6, n = 20", "m = -6, n = 44", "m = 6, n = -44"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Using the remainder theorem the given equation should be equal to zero when we put, </p><p>X + 2 = 0 =&gt; X = -2 </p><p>X  -  1 = 0 =&gt; X = 1 </p><p>If X = -2</p><p>2X<sup>3</sup> + 12X<sup>2</sup> + mX + n = 0</p><p>2 * (-2)<sup>3</sup> + 12 * (-2)<sup>2</sup> + m * -2 + n = 0 </p><p>n = 2m  -  32 .. (i)</p><p>If X = 1 </p><p>2X<sup>3</sup> + 12X<sup>2</sup> + mX + n = 0 </p><p>2 * 1<sup>3</sup> + 12 * 1<sup>2</sup> + m * 1 + n = 0 </p><p>m + n + 14 = 0 .. (ii) </p><p>from (i) and (ii) </p><p>m + 2m  -  32 + 14 = 0 </p><p>m = 6 </p><p>n = -20 </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Using the remainder theorem the given equation should be equal to zero when we put, </p><p>X + 2 = 0 =&gt; X = -2 </p><p>X  -  1 = 0 =&gt; X = 1 </p><p>If X = -2</p><p>2X<sup>3</sup> + 12X<sup>2</sup> + mX + n = 0</p><p>2 * (-2)<sup>3</sup> + 12 * (-2)<sup>2</sup> + m * -2 + n = 0 </p><p>n = 2m  -  32 .. (i)</p><p>If X = 1 </p><p>2X<sup>3</sup> + 12X<sup>2</sup> + mX + n = 0 </p><p>2 * 1<sup>3</sup> + 12 * 1<sup>2</sup> + m * 1 + n = 0 </p><p>m + n + 14 = 0 .. (ii) </p><p>from (i) and (ii) </p><p>m + 2m  -  32 + 14 = 0 </p><p>m = 6 </p><p>n = -20 </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>A sum of money at simple rate of interest amounts to Rs. 689 in 3 years and Rs. 901 in 7 years. Find the principal amount.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2342;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; 3 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 689 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; 7 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 901 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2343;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["Rs. 640", "Rs. 600", "Rs. 550", "Rs. 530"], "options_hi": ["640 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "600 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "550 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "530 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Interest obtained in 4 years = 901  -  689 = Rs. 212</p><p>Interest obtained in 3 years = 212/4 * 3 = Rs. 159</p><p>Principal amount = 689  -  159 = Rs. 530</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Interest obtained in 4 years = 901  -  689 = Rs. 212</p><p>Interest obtained in 3 years = 212/4 * 3 = Rs. 159</p><p>Principal amount = 689  -  159 = Rs. 530</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the ratio in which two varieties of gram costing Rs. 60/kg and Rs. 90/kg be mixed to get a mixture worth of Rs. 72/kg.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>60 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2324;&#2352; 90 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2330;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2350;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319; &#2325;&#2367; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; 72 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["3 : 4", "5 : 3", "2 : 1", "3 : 2"], "options_hi": ["3 : 4", "5 : 3", "2 : 1", "3 : 2"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p><img width=303 height=191 id=\"Picture 2\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22892/image001.png\"></p><p>Required ratio = 18 : 12 = 3 : 2</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=303 height=191 id=\"Picture 2\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22892/image001.png\"></p><p>Required ratio = 18 : 12 = 3 : 2</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>3/17<sup>th</sup> part of a work can be done by A in 18 days. Find the total number of days taken by A to complete the whole work.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; 3/17&#2357;&#2366;&#2306; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; A &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; 18 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2360;&#2306;&#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; A &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["85", "102", "91", "68"], "options_hi": ["85", "102", "91", "68"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>3/17<sup>th</sup> part of the work can be completed in 18 days.</p><p>So, whole work can be completed in 18 * 17/3 = 102 days</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>3/17<sup>th</sup> part of the work can be completed in 18 days.</p><p>So, whole work can be completed in 18 * 17/3 = 102 days</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time & Work"}, {"q_en": "<p>If 5 <sup>(a + b) </sup>= 125 and 25 <sup>(a  -  b) </sup>= 625, find the value of 2a.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 5 <sup>(a + b) </sup>= 125 &#2324;&#2352; 25 <sup>(a - b) </sup>= 625, &#2340;&#2379; 2a &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["10", "5", "8", "1"], "options_hi": ["10", "5", "8", "1"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img width=97 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image001.png\"></p><p><img width=117 height=23 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image002.png\"></p><p><img width=109 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image003.png\"></p><p><img width=116 height=23 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image004.png\"></p><p><img width=117 height=23 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image005.png\"></p><p><img width=37 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image006.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=97 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image001.png\"></p><p><img width=117 height=23 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image002.png\"></p><p><img width=109 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image003.png\"></p><p><img width=116 height=23 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image004.png\"></p><p><img width=117 height=23 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image005.png\"></p><p><img width=37 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image006.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>A vessel contains 18 litres mixture of milk and water in the ratio 5:1. If 3 litres of milk is added to the vessel, then how much water (in litres) should be added to the vessel to have milk and water in the ratio 9:2?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 5:1 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; 18 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 3 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; (&#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319; &#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2367; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 9:2 &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["2", "1.5", "0.5", "1"], "options_hi": ["2", "1.5", "0.5", "1"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Initial mixture = 18 litres </p><p>Milk = (5/6) * 18 = 15 litres </p><p>Water = (1/6) * 18 = 3 litres </p><p>Let x litres of water be added =&gt;</p><p>(15 + 3)/(3 + x) = 9/2</p><p>18 * 2 = 9(3 + x)</p><p>36 = 27 + 9x </p><p>9x = 9 </p><p>x = 1 </p><p>Hence, option 'd' is correct.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Initial mixture = 18 litres </p><p>Milk = (5/6) * 18 = 15 litres </p><p>Water = (1/6) * 18 = 3 litres </p><p>Let x litres of water be added =&gt;</p><p>(15 + 3)/(3 + x) = 9/2</p><p>18 * 2 = 9(3 + x)</p><p>36 = 27 + 9x </p><p>9x = 9 </p><p>x = 1 </p><p>Hence, option 'd' is correct.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixture & Alligation"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the value of given expression.</p><p>64  -  [(104 &div; 13) + (648 &div; 12)  -  (906 &div; 151)]</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2306;&#2332;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p><p>64 - [(104 &div; 13) + (648 &div; 12) - (906 &div; 151)]</p>", "options_en": ["11", "5", "8", "13"], "options_hi": ["11", "5", "8", "13"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>64  -  [(104 &div; 13) + (648 &div; 12)  -  (906 &div; 151)]</p><p>= 64  -  [8 + 54  -  6]</p><p>= 64  -  56</p><p>= 8</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>64  -  [(104 &div; 13) + (648 &div; 12)  -  (906 &div; 151)]</p><p>= 64  -  [8 + 54  -  6]</p><p>= 64  -  56</p><p>= 8</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>If the square of two times a boy's present age is decreased by sixteen times the present age of a boy, is equal to 240 more than the square of the present age of the boy, then the present age of the boy is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2310;&#2351;&#2369; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2310;&#2351;&#2369; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2379;&#2354;&#2361; &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379; &#2328;&#2335;&#2366; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;, &#2332;&#2379; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2310;&#2351;&#2369; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375; 240 &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2379;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2310;&#2351;&#2369; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["16 years", "12 years", "10 years", "14 years"], "options_hi": ["16 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;", "12 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;", "10 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;", "14 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let the present age of the boy be 'X' years</p><p>According to question,</p><p>(2X)<sup>2</sup>  -  16 * X = 240 + X<sup>2</sup></p><p>3X<sup>2</sup>  -  16X  -  240 = 0 </p><p>3X<sup>2</sup>  -  36X + 20X  -  240 = 0 </p><p>3X (X  -  12) + 20 (X  -  12) = 0 </p><p>(3X + 20) (X  -  12) = 0 </p><p>X = 12 [X &#8800; -20/3] </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the present age of the boy be 'X' years</p><p>According to question,</p><p>(2X)<sup>2</sup>  -  16 * X = 240 + X<sup>2</sup></p><p>3X<sup>2</sup>  -  16X  -  240 = 0 </p><p>3X<sup>2</sup>  -  36X + 20X  -  240 = 0 </p><p>3X (X  -  12) + 20 (X  -  12) = 0 </p><p>(3X + 20) (X  -  12) = 0 </p><p>X = 12 [X &#8800; -20/3] </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Simplify:</p><p><div><div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">3&radic;5 + &radic;20 &#8722; 2&radic;45", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2379; &#2360;&#2352;&#2354; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;:</p><p><div><div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">3&radic;5 + &radic;20 &#8722; 2&radic;45", "options_en": ["1", "&#8722;1", "2", "&#8722;2"], "options_hi": ["1", "&#8722;1", "2", "&#8722;2"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>&radic;20 = 2&radic;5, &radic;45 = 3&radic;5</p><p>Numerator = 3&radic;5 + 2&radic;5  -  2*3&radic;5 = (5&radic;5 &#8722; 6&radic;5) = &#8722;&radic;5</p><p>(3&radic;5 + &radic;20 &#8722; 2&radic;45) / &radic;5 = &#8722;&radic;5 / &radic;5 = &#8722;1</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>&radic;20 = 2&radic;5, &radic;45 = 3&radic;5</p><p>Numerator = 3&radic;5 + 2&radic;5  -  2*3&radic;5 = (5&radic;5 &#8722; 6&radic;5) = &#8722;&radic;5</p><p>(3&radic;5 + &radic;20 &#8722; 2&radic;45) / &radic;5 = &#8722;&radic;5 / &radic;5 = &#8722;1</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simplification"}, {"q_en": "<p>A ball of lead 4 cm in diameter is covered with gold. If the volume of the gold and lead are equal, then the thickness of gold[given <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005811.png\"/> = 1. 259] is approximately</p><p></p>", "q_hi": "<p>4 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2360; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2368;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2327;&#2375;&#2306;&#2342; &#2360;&#2379;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2375; &#2310;&#2357;&#2371;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2379;&#2344;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2368;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2360;&#2379;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2379;&#2335;&#2366;&#2312; [&#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005811.png\"> = 1. 259] &#2354;&#2327;&#2349;&#2327; &#2361;&#2376;-</p>", "options_en": ["5.038 cm", "5.190 cm", "1.038 cm", "0.518 cm"], "options_hi": ["5.038 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "5.190 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "1. 038 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "0.518 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "\"<p> Let the thickness of gold be r. </p><p> <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/fdfe4de571ff6b836ad6271695ecd967.png\" /> </p><p>Then volume of gold = volume of ball &#8211; volume of lead ball</p><p>Volume of gold </p><p> \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005532.png\"/>\r </p><p>Now, it is given that volume of gold </p><p>= Volume of lead ball </p><p> <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/487c938190880ae26b2d22405e864919.png\" /> </p><p></p>\"", "solution_hi": "\"<p> Let the thickness of gold be r. </p><p> <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/fdfe4de571ff6b836ad6271695ecd967.png\" /> </p><p>Then volume of gold = volume of ball &#8211; volume of lead ball</p><p>Volume of gold </p><p> \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005532.png\"/>\r </p><p>Now, it is given that volume of gold </p><p>= Volume of lead ball </p><p> <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/487c938190880ae26b2d22405e864919.png\" /> </p><p></p>\"", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>The average marks (out of 100) of boys and girls in an examination are 75 and 80, respectively. If the average marks of all the students in that examination are 78. Find the ratio of the number of boys to the number of girls.</p><p><b>Options:</b></p>", "q_hi": "&#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; (100 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375;) &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 75 &#2324;&#2352; 80 &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2313;&#2360; &#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; 78 &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p><p><b>&#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2381;&#2346;:</b>", "options_en": ["2:3", "3:4", "1:3", "1:2"], "options_hi": ["2:3", "3:4", "1:3", "1:2"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let the number of girls in the examination = X</p><p>Number of boys in the examination = 100  -  X</p><p>Average marks (out of 100) of boys and girls in an examination are 75 and 80 respectively.</p><p>ACQ,</p><p>75(100  -  X) + 80X = 78*100</p><p>7500  -  75X + 80X = 7800</p><p>5X = 300</p><p>X = 60</p><p>Required ratio = (100  -  60):60 = 2:3</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the number of girls in the examination = X</p><p>Number of boys in the examination = 100  -  X</p><p>Average marks (out of 100) of boys and girls in an examination are 75 and 80 respectively.</p><p>ACQ,</p><p>75(100  -  X) + 80X = 78*100</p><p>7500  -  75X + 80X = 7800</p><p>5X = 300</p><p>X = 60</p><p>Required ratio = (100  -  60):60 = 2:3</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Average"}, {"q_en": "<p>Two inlet pipes A and B and one outlet pipe C are attached to a tank and pipes A and B alone can fill the tank in 30 minutes and 42 minutes, respectively while pipe C alone can empty it in 18 minutes. If all the three are kept open simultaneously, when will the tank be full?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2311;&#2344;&#2354;&#2375;&#2335; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2313;&#2335;&#2354;&#2375;&#2335; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; C &#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2360;&#2375; &#2332;&#2369;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375; &#2361;&#2369;&#2319; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2309;&#2325;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 30 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2324;&#2352; 42 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2332;&#2348;&#2325;&#2367; &#2309;&#2325;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; C &#2311;&#2360;&#2375; 18 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2326;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2326;&#2369;&#2354;&#2366; &#2352;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2348; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2349;&#2352;&#2375;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["840 minutes", "420 minutes", "240 minutes", "630 minutes"], "options_hi": ["840 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "420 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "240 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "630 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Time is taken by A to fill the tank = 30 minutes</p><p>Time is taken by B to fill the tank = 42 minutes</p><p>Time is taken by C to empty the tank = 18 minutes</p><p>If all the three are kept open simultaneously,</p><p>Then tank will be filled in = 1/(1/30 + 1/42 - 1/18) = 630 minutes</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Time is taken by A to fill the tank = 30 minutes</p><p>Time is taken by B to fill the tank = 42 minutes</p><p>Time is taken by C to empty the tank = 18 minutes</p><p>If all the three are kept open simultaneously,</p><p>Then tank will be filled in = 1/(1/30 + 1/42 - 1/18) = 630 minutes</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Pipes & Cisterns"}, {"q_en": "<p>If the ratio of speed of boat in still water and speed of boat in downstream is 4: 5 and boat covers 96 km in upstream in 16 hours, then in how many hours boat can cover 112 km downstream?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2352; &#2332;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2324;&#2352; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 4:5 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; 96 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; 16 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; 112 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["10.2 hours", "3.6 hours", "5.4 hours", "11.2 hour"], "options_hi": ["10.2 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "3.6 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "5.4 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "11.2 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let speed of the boat in still water = 4x km/h and speed of boat in downstream = 5x</p><p>So, speed of the stream = 5x  -  4x = x km/h</p><p>So, upstream speed = 4x  -  x = 3x km/h</p><p>Upstream speed = 96/16 = 6 km/h</p><p>=&gt; x = 2</p><p>So, time taken by boat = 112/10 = 11.2 hours</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let speed of the boat in still water = 4x km/h and speed of boat in downstream = 5x</p><p>So, speed of the stream = 5x  -  4x = x km/h</p><p>So, upstream speed = 4x  -  x = 3x km/h</p><p>Upstream speed = 96/16 = 6 km/h</p><p>=&gt; x = 2</p><p>So, time taken by boat = 112/10 = 11.2 hours</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;If x = 7  -  4&radic;3, then find the value of x<sup>2</sup> +&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1", "q_hi": "<p><div>&nbsp;&#2351;&#2342;&#2367;  x = 7  -  4&radic;3, &#2340;&#2379; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;   x<sup>2</sup> +&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1", "options_en": ["188", "194", "186", "196"], "options_hi": ["188", "194", "186", "196"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Conjugate of x = 7 + 4&radic;3</p><p>x  X  (7 + 4&radic;3) = (7 - 4&radic;3)(7 + 4&radic;3)</p><p>=&gt; x  X  (7 + 4&radic;3) = 49 - (4&radic;3)<sup>2</sup></p><p>=&gt; 49  -  48 = 1</p><p>=&gt; 1/x = 7 + 4&radic;3</p><p>x + 1/x = (7 - 4&radic;3) + (7 + 4&radic;3)</p><p>=&gt; x + 1/x = 7 + 7 = 14</p><p>x<sup>2</sup> + 1/x<sup>2</sup> = (x + 1/x)<sup>2</sup> - 2</p><p>=&gt; x<sup>2</sup> + 1/x<sup>2</sup> = 14<sup>2</sup> - 2</p><p>=&gt; 196  -  2 = 194</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Conjugate of x = 7 + 4&radic;3</p><p>x  X  (7 + 4&radic;3) = (7 - 4&radic;3)(7 + 4&radic;3)</p><p>=&gt; x  X  (7 + 4&radic;3) = 49 - (4&radic;3)<sup>2</sup></p><p>=&gt; 49  -  48 = 1</p><p>=&gt; 1/x = 7 + 4&radic;3</p><p>x + 1/x = (7 - 4&radic;3) + (7 + 4&radic;3)</p><p>=&gt; x + 1/x = 7 + 7 = 14</p><p>x<sup>2</sup> + 1/x<sup>2</sup> = (x + 1/x)<sup>2</sup> - 2</p><p>=&gt; x<sup>2</sup> + 1/x<sup>2</sup> = 14<sup>2</sup> - 2</p><p>=&gt; 196  -  2 = 194</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>18 workers can complete a piece of work in 96 days. They start working together and after 26 days 10 more workers join them. In how many days in all will the work be completed?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>18 &#2350;&#2332;&#2342;&#2370;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2379; 96 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2357;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2366; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; 26 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; 10 &#2324;&#2352; &#2350;&#2332;&#2342;&#2370;&#2352; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2332;&#2369;&#2337;&#2364; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["69", "71", "72", "70"], "options_hi": ["69", "71", "72", "70"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Total work = 18 * 96 = 1728 worker-days</p><p>Work done in 26 days by 18 workers = 18 * 26 = 468 worker-days</p><p>Remaining work = 1728 - 468 = 1260 worker-days</p><p>Days for remaining work = 1260/(18 + 10) = 45 days</p><p>Total days = 26 + 45 = 71 days</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total work = 18 * 96 = 1728 worker-days</p><p>Work done in 26 days by 18 workers = 18 * 26 = 468 worker-days</p><p>Remaining work = 1728 - 468 = 1260 worker-days</p><p>Days for remaining work = 1260/(18 + 10) = 45 days</p><p>Total days = 26 + 45 = 71 days</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>What is the mode of 71,71, 72, 73, 77, 80, 85, 85, 78, 79, 73, 77, 80, 77, 75, 73, 75, 79, 77, 73, 74, 75, 77, 75?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>71,71, 72, 73, 77, 80, 85, 85, 78, 79, 73, 77, 80, 77, 75, 73, 75, 79, 77, 73, 74, 75, 77, 75 &#2325;&#2366; &#2348;&#2361;&#2369;&#2354;&#2325; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["73", "77", "75", "79"], "options_hi": ["73", "77", "75", "79"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Frequency of term 77 is 5 and it is highest among the given terms.</p><p>So, mode of the data is 77.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Frequency of term 77 is 5 and it is highest among the given terms.</p><p>So, mode of the data is 77.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Statistics"}, {"q_en": "<p>LCM of two numbers is 12 times of the HCF of the numbers and sum of LCM and HCF of numbers is 208. If one number is 48, then find the other number.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; LCM &#2313;&#2344; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; HCF &#2325;&#2366; 12 &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; LCM &#2324;&#2352; HCF &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; 208 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 48 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["44", "46", "64", "54"], "options_hi": ["44", "46", "64", "54"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let the other number be a and HCF of numbers be x</p><p>Then LCM of numbers = 12x</p><p>According to question,</p><p>x + 12x = 208</p><p>x = 208/13 = 16</p><p>LCM = 16 * 12 = 192</p><p>LCM * HCF = Products of two numbers</p><p>16 * 192 = 48 * a</p><p>a = (16 * 192)/48</p><p>a = 64</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the other number be a and HCF of numbers be x</p><p>Then LCM of numbers = 12x</p><p>According to question,</p><p>x + 12x = 208</p><p>x = 208/13 = 16</p><p>LCM = 16 * 12 = 192</p><p>LCM * HCF = Products of two numbers</p><p>16 * 192 = 48 * a</p><p>a = (16 * 192)/48</p><p>a = 64</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "HCF & LCM"}, {"q_en": "<p>From two points located X meters and Y meters away from the base of a building on the same straight line (such that Y>X), the angles of elevation to the top of the building are supplementary. If the angle of elevation from the point C is 45&deg; which is X meters away from the base of a building,  and the height of the building is h meters, find the value of the product X * Y.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2311;&#2350;&#2366;&#2352;&#2340; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; X &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; Y &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2361;&#2368; &#2360;&#2368;&#2343;&#2368; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2342;&#2379; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369;&#2323;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; (&#2332;&#2376;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367; Y>X), &#2311;&#2350;&#2366;&#2352;&#2340; &#2325;&#2375; &#2358;&#2368;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2346;&#2352; &#2313;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; C &#2360;&#2375; &#2313;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; 45 &#2337;&#2367;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2379; &#2311;&#2350;&#2366;&#2352;&#2340; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; X &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2350;&#2366;&#2352;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; h &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2344;&#2347;&#2354; X * Y &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["2h", "h/2", "h<sup>2</sup>", "-h<sup>2</sup>"], "options_hi": ["2h", "h/2", "h<sup>2</sup>", "-h<sup>2</sup>"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p><img width=272 height=208 id=image1.png src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27673/image001.jpg\" alt=O46.JPG></p><p>In triangle ABC,</p><p>tan 45&deg; = h/X</p><p>X = h</p><p>In triangle ADB,</p><p>tan 135&deg; = h/Y</p><p>-1 = h/Y</p><p>Y = -h</p><p>Required product = X* Y = h* (-h) = -h<sup>2</sup>.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=272 height=208 id=image1.png src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27673/image001.jpg\" alt=O46.JPG></p><p>In triangle ABC,</p><p>tan 45&deg; = h/X</p><p>X = h</p><p>In triangle ADB,</p><p>tan 135&deg; = h/Y</p><p>-1 = h/Y</p><p>Y = -h</p><p>Required product = X* Y = h* (-h) = -h<sup>2</sup>.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Height & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>The graph of 5x = 7 + 2y cuts the x  -  axis at point P(a, b). Find the value of (2a  -  3b).</p>", "q_hi": "<p>5x = 7 + 2y &#2325;&#2366; &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2347; x - &#2309;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2379; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; P(a, b) &#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366;&#2335;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; (2a - 3b) &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["12/5", "17/5", "9/5", "14/5"], "options_hi": ["12/5", "17/5", "9/5", "14/5"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Since, the graph of 5x = 7 + 2y cuts the x  -  axis at point P(a, b).</p><p>So, y = 0 =&gt; b = 0</p><p>5x = 7 + 2*0</p><p>x = 7/5</p><p>a = 7/5</p><p>2a  -  3b = 2*7/5  -  3*0 </p><p>= 14/5</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Since, the graph of 5x = 7 + 2y cuts the x  -  axis at point P(a, b).</p><p>So, y = 0 =&gt; b = 0</p><p>5x = 7 + 2*0</p><p>x = 7/5</p><p>a = 7/5</p><p>2a  -  3b = 2*7/5  -  3*0 </p><p>= 14/5</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Calculate the mode from the following data.</p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Days of confinement</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">6</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">7</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">8</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">9</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">10</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Number of patients</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">4</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">6</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">7</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">5</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">3</td></tr></table>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2337;&#2375;&#2335;&#2366; &#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2361;&#2369;&#2354;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2339;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">&#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366;&#2357;&#2366;&#2360; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">6</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">7</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">8</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">9</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">10</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">&#2350;&#2352;&#2368;&#2332;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">4</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">6</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">7</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">5</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">3</td></tr></table>", "options_en": ["8", "7", "5", "6"], "options_hi": ["8", "7", "5", "6"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Highest number of patients = 7</p><p>Mode = Days of confinement for 7 patients = 8</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Highest number of patients = 7</p><p>Mode = Days of confinement for 7 patients = 8</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Statistics"}, {"q_en": "<p>A vessel contains 1600 litres of milk. 320 litres of milk was taken out from it and replaced with water. Then again from the mixture, 320 litres is taken out and replaced with water. The ratio of milk and water in the resultant mixture is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 1600 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; 320 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366;&#2354;&#2325;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2327;&#2361; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2337;&#2366;&#2354; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2347;&#2367;&#2352; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2360;&#2375; 320 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366;&#2354;&#2325;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2327;&#2361; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2337;&#2366;&#2354; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2339;&#2366;&#2350;&#2368; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["16: 9", "9: 5", "12: 11", "15: 13"], "options_hi": ["16: 9", "9: 5", "12: 11", "15: 13"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>a = Initial quantity </p><p>b = amount removed and replaced </p><p>n = number of times </p><p>Final Quantity = a * (1  -  b/a)<sup>n</sup></p><p>= 1600 * (1  -  320/1600)<sup>2</sup></p><p>= 1600 * 4/5 * 4/5</p><p>= 1024 l</p><p>Water = 1600  -  1024 = 576 l</p><p>Hence, the required ratio = 1024/576 = 16:9</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>a = Initial quantity </p><p>b = amount removed and replaced </p><p>n = number of times </p><p>Final Quantity = a * (1  -  b/a)<sup>n</sup></p><p>= 1600 * (1  -  320/1600)<sup>2</sup></p><p>= 1600 * 4/5 * 4/5</p><p>= 1024 l</p><p>Water = 1600  -  1024 = 576 l</p><p>Hence, the required ratio = 1024/576 = 16:9</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixture & Alligation"}, {"q_en": "<p>On a circular path of 595 m, Anil and Billa start walking from the same point but in the opposite direction at the speed of 3.45 km/h and 2.5 km/h, respectively. When they will meet for the first time?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>595 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2346;&#2341; &#2346;&#2352;, &#2309;&#2344;&#2367;&#2354; &#2324;&#2352; &#2348;&#2367;&#2354;&#2381;&#2354;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2361;&#2368; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2360;&#2375; &#2354;&#2375;&#2325;&#2367;&#2344; &#2357;&#2367;&#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2340; &#2342;&#2367;&#2358;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 3.45 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; 2.5 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; &#2330;&#2354;&#2344;&#2366; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2357;&#2375; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2368; &#2348;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2348; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2375;&#2306;&#2327;&#2375;?</p>", "options_en": ["After 6 minutes", "After 9 minutes", "After 8 minutes", "After 11 minutes"], "options_hi": ["6 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342;", "9 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342;", "8 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342;", "11 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Relative speed = 3.45 + 2.5 = 5.95 kmph</p><p>Required time = (595/1000)/5.95</p><p>= 1/10 hours</p><p>= After 6 minutes</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Relative speed = 3.45 + 2.5 = 5.95 kmph</p><p>Required time = (595/1000)/5.95</p><p>= 1/10 hours</p><p>= After 6 minutes</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the value of:</p><p><div><div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1", "q_hi": "<p><div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1", "options_en": ["0", "2", "1", "5"], "options_hi": ["0", "2", "1", "5"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "\"<p> <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-000100.png\"/> </p><p> <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-006357.png\"/> </p>\"", "solution_hi": "\"<p> <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-000100.png\"/> </p><p> <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-006357.png\"/> </p>\"", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simplification"}, {"q_en": "<p>10 years ago, the age of Sunita was thrice the age of her daughter Tanya. 10 years hence, the age of Sunita will be twice the age of Tanya. What is the ratio of their present ages?</p>", "q_hi": "10 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2375;, &#2360;&#2369;&#2344;&#2368;&#2340;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351;&#2369; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2348;&#2375;&#2335;&#2368; &#2340;&#2366;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351;&#2369; &#2360;&#2375; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2341;&#2368;&#2404; 10 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342;, &#2360;&#2369;&#2344;&#2368;&#2340;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351;&#2369; &#2340;&#2366;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351;&#2369; &#2360;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379;&#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2327;&#2368;&#2404; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2310;&#2351;&#2369; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?", "options_en": ["3 : 7", "7 : 3", "2 : 7", "7 : 2"], "options_hi": ["3 : 7", "7 : 3", "2 : 7", "7 : 2"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let the age of Tanya 10 years ago = x</p><p>Then age of Sunita before 10 years ago = 3x</p><p>Also, 3x + 20 = 2(x + 20)</p><p>3x + 20 = 2x + 40</p><p>x = 20</p><p>present age of Sunita = 3*20 + 10 = 70 years</p><p>present age of Tanya = 20 + 10 = 30 years</p><p>required ratio = 70 : 30 = 7 : 3</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the age of Tanya 10 years ago = x</p><p>Then age of Sunita before 10 years ago = 3x</p><p>Also, 3x + 20 = 2(x + 20)</p><p>3x + 20 = 2x + 40</p><p>x = 20</p><p>present age of Sunita = 3*20 + 10 = 70 years</p><p>present age of Tanya = 20 + 10 = 30 years</p><p>required ratio = 70 : 30 = 7 : 3</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}]}